      "edition": "Saturday 21 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Stuart effect",
          "heading": "Will Stuart back from ruptured Achilles as England chase All Black scalp",
          "body": "The BBC's Mike Henson ties England's revival to Will Stuart, the England and British and Irish Lions star who missed the start of the year with a ruptured Achilles tendon. Without him England endured a terrible Six Nations and five straight defeats. Since his return they have scored 20 tries against Australia and Japan and sit top of the Nations Championship for points scored and entries into the opposition 22. Saturday's visitors arrive sore after a first defeat by Wales in 73 years."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France beat Springboks 21-19",
