    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-21",
      "edition": "Saturday 21 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Pumas warning",
          "heading": "Marc Duzan warns France against underestimating struggling Pumas after Springbok win",
          "body": "Midi Olympique senior reporter Marc Duzan concedes the Pumas arrive in poor shape: eighth in the world rankings, they were beaten 42-12 by Ireland a fortnight ago, lost 14-19 in Italy last weekend and are without the injured Juan Cruz Mallía, whom he rates their best player. Writing in Rugbyrama after France's 21-19 defeat of the Springboks at Saint-Denis, he nonetheless calls taking them lightly an enormous mistake. Victory would earn the Bleus a Nations Championship final at Twickenham the following weekend."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland's Sam Illo ruled out of Springboks Test with concussion",
