    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-21",
      "edition": "Saturday 21 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Captain's call",
          "heading": "Nicotera admits Italy's low spell, eyes Fiji test to rebuild confidence",
          "body": "Italy captain Giacomo Nicotera admitted at his pre-match press conference that the squad still carry a nagging frustration from defeats by South Africa and Argentina, two games he called emotionally hard for different reasons. Calling it a low spell, he said Italy need one match to rediscover positive feelings and confidence. On Saturday's opponents in Udine, the Trieste native called Fiji a more approachable match, true to the world rankings, but warned of incredible individuals playing in France's Top 14."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France beat Springboks 21-19",
          "body": "Ireland's Sam Illo ruled out of Springboks Test with concussion. Scotland's Rory Darge withdraws from Japan Test with shoulder injury."
