      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Captaincy switch",
          "heading": "Stafford McDowall to captain Scotland against Japan as Rory Darge withdraws injured",
          "body": "Head coach Gregor Townsend has changed captain for the second time in a week. Forward Rory Darge, man of the match against Australia while standing in for the ruled-out Sione Tuipulotu, was initially named despite a shoulder injury but will now sit out today's test, the BBC reports. Glasgow centre Stafford McDowall takes the armband six days after being called off his father's farm in Dumfries to face the Wallabies. Matt Fagerson starts at No. 8. Darge stays in the squad, aiming to play next week."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France beat Springboks 21-19",
