    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-21",
      "edition": "Saturday 21 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "2007 revisited",
          "heading": "Fabien Pelous recalls Pumas beating hosts France twice at 2007 World Cup",
          "body": "France hosted a World Cup for the first time in 2007, and it began and ended with defeat to Argentina — in the opening match at the Stade de France and again in the third-place play-off. Fabien Pelous, 33 and on his last campaign with France, says the hosts were lulled by home enthusiasm and the Pumas got inside their heads, playing hard, ball-hoarding rugby like Bernard Laporte's Stade Français. Agustín Pichot, scrum-half and captain, did everything to unsettle opposite number Jean-Baptiste Elissalde."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France beat Springboks 21-19",
