      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Eligibility watch",
          "heading": "Les Kiss keeps eye on Liam Wright as Wales eligibility looms",
          "body": "Former Wallabies captain Liam Wright, now an Ospreys flanker, visited the Australia camp in Cardiff this week. Australia head coach Les Kiss, who coached him at the Queensland Reds, did not rule out a recall: \"And someone of his calibre, we'll keep an eye on for sure.\" The 29-year-old has six caps, the last as captain against Wales in July 2024. He becomes Welsh-qualified next summer through a Pembroke Dock grandfather. Wright says he wants a gold jersey but would explore Wales if that door closes."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France beat Springboks 21-19",
