      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury toll",
          "heading": "Japan lose Takeuchi, Tokito and props Tamafusa and Helu before Murrayfield",
          "body": "All four are out through injury or condition for Saturday's Nations Championship finale against Scotland, Rugby Asia 247 reports. With both props unavailable, Sojiro Otsuka, Kenji Sato and Ryosuke Iwaihara start up front, while Toyota Verblitz call-up Taufa Latu takes the No. 18 shirt. History offers little comfort: Scotland have won eight of the nine meetings, Japan's lone victory coming at their home 2019 World Cup, and the hosts won 29-20 when the sides last met in Edinburgh."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France beat Springboks 21-19",
