    "465": {
      "date": "2026-11-21",
      "edition": "Saturday 21 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Boardroom pressure",
          "heading": "David Kirk puts Dave Rennie's All Blacks on notice before England Test",
          "body": "NZ Rugby chair David Kirk says he would be \"pretty disappointed\" by defeat at Twickenham, but will judge head coach Dave Rennie's side on performance rather than result: \"a bad loss would be concerning.\" Kirk called this the All Blacks' hardest year, with three of their four defeats coming against the Springboks. He described the fourth, last weekend's 28-35 loss in Cardiff, as a Welsh miracle, and noted New Zealand had just one scrum put-in. Rennie's predecessor, Scott Robertson, was sacked after a loss to England."
